From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:00:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Leave the status block as it was when setting file
 information fails.

Windows does not write the IO_STATUS_BLOCK of an NtSetInformationFile call
that fails with an error status; the tests check io.Status is still
0xdeadbeef after a rename, link or completion request is refused, and
16 of those checks pass now.  The wow64 thunk wrote its own errors into
the block from a 64-bit block it had never set up, so a 32-bit caller
got the status with a stack address for Information; it returns them
without touching the block, as the other wow64 thunks do.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

